      "id": "65164983-33ef-482d-821b-3e1586cf594a",
      "name": "Settings",
      "description": {
        "content": "Vendor-level reference data, including the picklist endpoint\nthat supplies the acceptable values for opportunity fields.",
        "type": "text/plain"
      },
      "item": [
        {
          "id": "1b59799d-2193-4172-b872-4995a310f2ba",
          "name": "Get picklist options for Opportunity fields",
          "request": {
            "name": "Get picklist options for Opportunity fields",
            "description": {
              "content": "Returns the acceptable values for enumerable `Opportunity`\nfields, plus reference lists for country, language, and\ncurrency codes. Use this endpoint to populate picklist UI\ncontrols so that the values an integrator surfaces stay in\nstep with the values the API accepts (which can be a subset\nof the corresponding schema enum — see the `PicklistOptions`\nschema for details).\n\nThe response is an object keyed by field path\n(for example `.customerInfo.customerDetails.address.regionCode`);\neach value is the array of acceptable\n`{ display, value }` options for that field.\n\nThe response also contains a `.dataMapper.stage` key. This key\nis a curated subset of the `Stage` enum used by Tackle's Data\nMapper feature when importing opportunity data from external\nsystems. It does not correspond to any field on the\n`Opportunity` payload, and most integrators using this API\ndirectly can ignore it.\n\nRequires the `cosell:GetPicklistOptions` permission.",
              "type": "text/plain"
            },
            "url": {
              "path": [
                "api",
                "settings",
                "picklist-options"
              ],
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "query": [],
              "variable": []
            },
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "method": "GET",
            "auth": null
          },
          "response": [
